# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/

# Canonical: apex sitetrace.it.com is the primary domain.
# All www.sitetrace.it.com URLs 301 to the apex, path preserved.
# (AdSense and Google Search Console will index the apex; users typing www. get there too.)
https://www.sitetrace.it.com/*   https://sitetrace.it.com/:splat   301

# Convenience: trailing-slash normalization (Pages already does this; here for safety)
/home                /                  301
/tools               /                  301

# Old hash-routed URLs (from the previous single-page version) — redirect
# to the new per-tool pages for SEO. 301 = permanent.
# NOTE: hash-fragment sources are technically invalid (clients never send #frag
# to the server) and Cloudflare's _redirects parser appears to mis-match them,
# causing the root URL to 301 to /what-is-my-ip/. Keeping these as no-op
# comments to preserve intent documentation.
#/#/home              /what-is-my-ip/    301
#/#/ping              /ping/             301
#/#/dns               /dns-tools/        301
